<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib252800de20c886aafce65d4fd6f4b7f2dbe8473" commit="65a1855ca96526371b45190d7c875d804cb26f17" commit_message="dediprog: Leave standalone mode for SF600  Some Dediprog programmers have the ability to operate in &quot;standalone&quot; mode which does not need to be attached to a host computer via USB. We must disable this for Flashrom to be able to flash the SPI chip via USB.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=built and read firmware, didn't seem to make things worse...  Change-Id: Ib252800de20c886aafce65d4fd6f4b7f2dbe8473 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313018 Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="313018" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/18/313018/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I48fe0791e59721f99525750d3ef8daa026035098" commit="33eda556afa8046b6dc99bfa8abc092cbfe26ebb" commit_message="flashchips: Add function to populate list of voltage ranges  This can be used to attempt to find the supply voltage of a flash chip. It is intended for use with external programmers so that the user does not always need to set a voltage parameter.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=tested with follow-up patch for dediprog  Change-Id: I48fe0791e59721f99525750d3ef8daa026035098 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313019 Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="313019" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/19/313019/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8803b0d0aee3e0b551153209480041870ddf444e" commit="f92c45fa1fbc9083b5a757a82676575c208ba22b" commit_message="dediprog: Automatically detect SPI flash voltage  This makes the Dediprog automatically detect the SPI flash voltage, starting with the lowest value.  It uses the probe_flash() function to try and positively identify a chip by its manufacturer and device ID.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=Tested with W25Q32DW (1.8V) and W25Q64FV (3.3V)  Change-Id: I8803b0d0aee3e0b551153209480041870ddf444e Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313050 Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="313050" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/50/313050/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="If4f190a3b6c91638f89535e610c70b2417707031" commit="8ffe769065f9fca3a81560ffcd2f6d35fcadcd91" commit_message="PRIVATE: mesh: populate hop_count in mpath structure  Fix the issue by populating the field along with other mpath attributes. This information is being exported as part of mesh routing statistics.  BUG=b:26965392 TEST=manually on whirlwind  Change-Id: If4f190a3b6c91638f89535e610c70b2417707031 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328733 Commit-Ready: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328733" owner_email="julanhsu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/328733/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Icd142d04422a05366dce57a46156738031c7b780" commit="bcc5563cfcbe996407807bc9ca72160eba2718d0" commit_message="PRIVATE: mesh: export mesh routing stats to debugfs  Collect relevant mesh routing/path statistics. Add debugfs entry to display mesh path statistics. Sampling frequency is 1 second. Add a 1sec timer to calculate the statistics.  cat netdev:mesh-5000mhz/destinations/${mac_addr}/mesh_path_stats to display stats. echo reset &gt; mesh_path_stats to reset all values. (Note. due to the implementation using a common denominator, it does not make sense to reset individual statistic separately.)  BUG=b:26965392 TESTING=manually on whirlwind  Change-Id: Icd142d04422a05366dce57a46156738031c7b780 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328732 Commit-Ready: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328732" owner_email="julanhsu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/32/328732/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1c8b02908a34b7183e5d31d036d84f155c128384" commit="5b5cdf09c8f3bf139f70321c0675bcd61cb01276" commit_message="CRAS: iodev_list - Fix redundant NodesChanged signal  A call to cras_iodev_list_notify_nodes_changed() was added to synchronize device list to system state whenever node attribute is changed. However this introduced redundant NodesChanged signal sent to Chrome, and caused confusion. Fix this by spcifically update device list in every notify call for node attribute change.  BUG=None TEST=dbus-monitor to verity there is no redundant NodeChanged signal when adjusting volume. dbus-send consecutive methods: SetOutputNodeVolume and GetNodes, to verity the later method returns correct volume value set by the former.  Change-Id: I1c8b02908a34b7183e5d31d036d84f155c128384 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329454 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329454" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/54/329454/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9209436bf8c463638256779357d3b7af57a2d671" commit="03cc50029408a5b126382adfdd6b208aed2f12bb" commit_message="CRAS: test_client - Print stable_id of node  The stable_id of iodev is not used by Chrome at all. Change to print node's stable_id for debugging.  BUG=None TEST=cras_test_client --dump_s  Change-Id: I9209436bf8c463638256779357d3b7af57a2d671 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329455 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329455" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/55/329455/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0d38827e7334367939c79d53a97436f49bb7d575" commit="9a83196305009a6f44f7f0c8cc258d5c6d820c97" commit_message="Get chameleon log from board to test's output directory  Register get log function by atexit module. We will get all chameleon boards' log to output_directory/chameleond/chameleon-hostname/log .  BUG=chromium:504177 TEST=run suite:chameleon_dp, suite:chameleon_dp_stress      to see if we can get chameleond log for each test.  Change-Id: I0d38827e7334367939c79d53a97436f49bb7d575 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324744 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="324744" owner_email="mojahsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/44/324744/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib4fb1514cdfd9b5dbdfd1f04d9258807e33723f7" commit="d19be91ec41e5329fa32a3f85564c3c7b847abd8" commit_message="[removable_storage] Add option to use toybox dd  For current toybox in chromebook, the dd function in toybox is still under developing. So add a option to use toybox dd or not.  BUG=None TEST=test it manually on chromebook  Change-Id: Ib4fb1514cdfd9b5dbdfd1f04d9258807e33723f7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328949 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="328949" owner_email="mojahsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/49/328949/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3664fb669c81bcc1370c41ccc42494e8c2f4f19a" commit="423c77c5c2d70bc3601376767f8210123c53604b" commit_message="stressapptest: Add flag for use free memory only or total memory  For the case of tests using stressapptest for &quot;memory validation&quot;, it should test give ratio according to system total memory (and abort if the condition can't meet). However for devices on run-in rack, they may be running multiple stress tests in parallel - for example stressapptest (for CPU &amp; RAM), glbench (for GPU), and other tests for network or audio. And we can't expect how much memory will be free at that time - so using the ration for &quot;free memory&quot; would be the better idea.  This change adds a new argument to specify should we use only free memory or not (i.e., total memory).  BUG=None TEST=Run stressapptest on Lucid.  Change-Id: I3664fb669c81bcc1370c41ccc42494e8c2f4f19a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327449 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="327449" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/49/327449/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I22e02c46adf4c26ce70b42f350c1d50702fd64b5" commit="905f38713297c01de1b4394ade34b375f4ca56a0" commit_message="[ExtDisplay] Fix checking USB port status for connected  In dolphin case, the role of the USB port is 'SNK DFP' not 'SRC'. We remove the role checking for unpredicatable role's status. Only check connected status of the USB port. Fix lint error of lamda =&gt; def.  BUG=None TEST=test on chromebook manually  Change-Id: I22e02c46adf4c26ce70b42f350c1d50702fd64b5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328890 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="328890" owner_email="mojahsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/90/328890/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9e0748f2e2292c1b91c15a2929f5eb482dc18e9f" commit="14545308c01a178f29d2a68b605aef216b653255" commit_message="Prelabel the init binary with SELinux context.  This change uses the setfiles tool to set an SELinux context on the init binary when the OS image is built.  BUG=b:25408463 TEST=I built the OS, installed it, and ran ls -Z /sbin/init CQ-DEPEND=CL:*249719,CL:329413  Change-Id: I9e0748f2e2292c1b91c15a2929f5eb482dc18e9f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329184 Commit-Ready: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Greg Kerr &lt;kerrnel@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="329184" owner_email="kerrnel@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/84/329184/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id5db6a4ae5328b4d1416939cda6b0b77c90ab2e3" commit="425b90be03b3bd63c6fa13341410468f1116eec4" commit_message="[Dolphin] Add force DP negotitated argument.  Some DUTs need the renegotiation to recognize the DP interface. Add argument fire_hpd_manually for HPD control. Fix some lint problems.  BUG=None TEST=manaually test on chromebook  Change-Id: Id5db6a4ae5328b4d1416939cda6b0b77c90ab2e3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328585 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pin-chih Lin &lt;johnylin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="328585" owner_email="mojahsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromium